; The "punctured slab": conditioning on (z = 5 AND 2z ≠ 10) looks
; pointwise contradictory, but under the ε-limit semantics it is not:
; the exclusion's slab (ε/2 wide in 2z, i.e. ε/4 in z) is strictly
; narrower than the equality's (ε/2 in z), so the acceptance region is
; an annulus of width ε/2 whose weak limit is still δ₅. The evidence
; carries half the count of a plain (real_eq z 5.0), and the posterior
; over z is Dirac(5) — NOT the zero measure.
(query
  (let (z (gaussian 0.0 1.0))
    (Posterior z (and (real_eq z 5.0)
                      (not (real_eq (*. 2.0 z) 10.0))))))
